# DocuChat AI — Implementation Prompt

Analyze `docuchat-ai-prd.md` thoroughly and use it as the **single source of truth** for designing and implementing the DocuChat AI web application.

Follow the PRD’s architecture, technology choices, requirements, and security constraints. Do not introduce major architectural changes without asking me first.

## Development Process

Execute the project in **4 sequential phases**. **Do not proceed to the next phase until I explicitly approve it.**

### Phase 1 — UI/UX Only

Design and implement the complete frontend UI.

Focus exclusively on:

* Layout and information architecture
* Responsive design
* Component hierarchy
* Navigation
* Dashboard
* Document management UI
* PDF viewer UI
* Chat interface
* Message components
* Citation/source components
* Upload UI
* Processing/progress states
* Empty states
* Loading/skeleton states
* Error states
* Settings/profile UI
* Mobile/tablet/desktop layouts
* Accessibility
* Visual consistency

Use realistic mock/static data where necessary.

**Do NOT implement:**

* Database logic
* API calls
* Authentication logic
* Authorization logic
* Pinecone
* Gemini
* RAG
* File processing
* Background jobs
* Backend services
* Persistent data

The UI should be fully navigable using mocked data so the complete user experience can be evaluated before backend integration.

Use:

* [ui-ux-pro-max](slashCommand;ui-ux-pro-max) 
* [emil-design-eng](slashCommand;emil-design-eng) 

to guide the UI/UX and design-engineering decisions.

Prioritize:

* Strong visual hierarchy
* Clean modern design
* Excellent typography
* Consistent spacing
* Responsive behavior
* Accessibility
* Realistic product UX
* Production-quality component design

Before finishing Phase 1, verify that the UI covers all major user flows described in the PRD.

**Stop after Phase 1 and ask for my approval before continuing.**

